{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.HyperchargeBatteryReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.HyperchargeBatteryReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.nucleon_hypercharge_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.nucleon_hypercharge_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L186-L189","doc":"The nucleon hypercharge is `+1` (i.e. `6Y = 6`) for both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.nucleon_hypercharge_eq_baryon_number","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.nucleon_hypercharge_eq_baryon_number","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L174-L184","doc":"**B1 is the `L = 0` restriction of B2-LH.**\n\nOn the nucleon doublet lepton number vanishes, so the GMN-forced hypercharge\nequals the baryon number -- and equals `+1` for *both* the proton and the\nneutron.  This is the same degeneracy the chapter records as falsifying the\nwrithe map: `Y` does not separate `p` from `n`, while the writhe does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.neutron","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L171-L172","doc":"Neutron: `Q = 0`, `I₃ = -1/2`, `B = 1`, `L = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.proton","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L168-L169","doc":"Proton: `Q = 1`, `I₃ = 1/2`, `B = 1`, `L = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.lh_hypercharge_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.lh_hypercharge_values","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L161-L166","doc":"The B2-LH targets, in the `6×` normalisation: `6Y = {2, 2, -6, -6}`,\ni.e. `Y = {+1/3, +1/3, -1, -1}` for `(u, d, νₑ, e⁻)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.lh_hypercharge_eq_baryon_sub_lepton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.lh_hypercharge_eq_baryon_sub_lepton","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L149-L159","doc":"**The left-handed battery is exactly `B - L`.**\n\nFor each of the four first-generation left-handed fermions, the hypercharge\nforced by Gell-Mann--Nishijima equals baryon number minus lepton number.\nPure integer arithmetic in the `6×` normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.electronL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.electronL","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L146-L147","doc":"Left-handed electron: `Q = -1`, `I₃ = -1/2`, `B = 0`, `L = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.nuEL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.nuEL","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L143-L144","doc":"Left-handed electron neutrino: `Q = 0`, `I₃ = 1/2`, `B = 0`, `L = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.downL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.downL","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L140-L141","doc":"Left-handed down quark: `Q = -1/3`, `I₃ = -1/2`, `B = 1/3`, `L = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.upL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.upL","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L137-L138","doc":"Left-handed up quark: `Q = 2/3`, `I₃ = 1/2`, `B = 1/3`, `L = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.gmn_sixHypercharge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.gmn_sixHypercharge","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L126-L131","doc":"`sixHypercharge` is not an independent stipulation: it is exactly what\nthe cleared Gell-Mann--Nishijima relation forces from `sixQ` and `sixI₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixBaryonMinusLepton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixBaryonMinusLepton","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L123-L124","doc":"Six times the anomaly-free combination `B - L`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixHypercharge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixHypercharge","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L119-L121","doc":"Six times the hypercharge forced by GMN: from `2Q = 2I₃ + Y` we get\n`Y = 2Q - 2I₃`, hence `6Y = 2·(6Q) - 2·(6I₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.instDecidableEqFermionCharges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.instDecidableEqFermionCharges","kind":"instance","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L115-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.instDecidableEqFermionCharges.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.instDecidableEqFermionCharges.decEq","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L115-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixL","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L114-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixB","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L113-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixI₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixI₃","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.sixQ","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L111-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges.mk","kind":"ctor","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FermionCharges","kind":"structure","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L107-L115","doc":"First-generation quantum numbers, stored as **six times** the physical\nvalue so every entry is an integer and no division ever occurs:\n`sixQ = 6Q`, `sixI₃ = 6I₃`, `sixB = 6B`, `sixL = 6L`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.rh_hypercharge_eq_two_mul_charge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.rh_hypercharge_eq_two_mul_charge","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L100-L105","doc":"The right-handed hypercharge forced by GMN at `I₃ = 0` is `2Q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.hypercharge_determined_of_isospin_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.hypercharge_determined_of_isospin_zero","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L83-L98","doc":"**The right-handed battery is an identity, not a test.**\n\nOn a weak singlet (`I₃ = 0`) the Gell-Mann--Nishijima relation determines\n`Y` outright from `Q`.  So two candidate hypercharge assignments that both\nsatisfy GMN against the *same* derived charge agree on every right-handed\nrow: the right-handed half of B2 has no discriminating power.\n\nNo characteristic hypothesis is needed -- in the cleared form `Y` is\nsubtracted out, never divided out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.GellMannNishijima","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.GellMannNishijima","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean#L74-L81","doc":"The Gell-Mann--Nishijima relation in **cleared (division-free)** form,\n`2Q = 2I₃ + Y`.\n\nEquivalent to the familiar `Q = I₃ + Y/2` whenever `2` is invertible, but\nstated so that it makes sense -- and the results below hold -- over an\narbitrary commutative ring, with no characteristic hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}